        "benefits_md": "> **Short-Term Skill Training:** \n\n\n- Training duration ranges from 1 week to 6 weeks.\n- Courses are modular and industry-oriented.\n\n> **Industry-Relevant Courses:**\n\n\n- Training provided in emerging sectors such as:\n\n  - Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning\n  - Cloud Computing\n  - Cyber Security\n  - CAD/CAM/CNC\n  - Hydraulics and Pneumatics\n  - Automobile Engineering\n  - Welding Technology\n  - Electronics and Electrical Systems\n  - Solar Technology\n  - Fashion Designing\n  - Aeronautical Structure\n\n\n> **Tailor-Made Training Programs:**\n\n\n- Courses are designed according to the requirements of industries and establishments.\n\n> **Skill Upgradation:**\n\n\n- Helps industrial workers, engineers, and technicians update skills with the latest technologies.\n\n> **Infrastructure Support:**\n\n\n- Access to workshops, laboratories, library, hostel, and training facilities.\n\n> **Affordable Fee Structure:**\n\n\n- Application Fee: \u20b9100/- per participant per course\n- Gymkhana Fee: \u20b910/- per course\n- Tuition Fee (Per Week):\n\n  - Government Departments: \u20b91,250/- (Regular), \u20b92,500/- (Tailor-made)\n  - Medium/Large Industries: \u20b92,000/- (Regular), \u20b94,000/- (Tailor-made)\n  - Small Scale Industries/Private Candidates: \u20b91,000/-\n  - Technical Institutes: \u20b91,000/- (Regular), \u20b92,000/- (Tailor-made)\n  - State Directorates: NIL\n\n\n> **Hostel Facility:**\n\n\n- Limited hostel available on a first-come, first-served basis.\n- Charges: \u20b9100/- per day per participant.\n\n> **Mode of Disbursement:** Training services are provided directly through NSTIs at Mumbai, Kanpur, Howrah, Hyderabad (Vidyanagar), Chennai, Hyderabad (Ramanthapur), Ludhiana, Dehradun, Calicut, Bangalore, Jamshedpur, and other centres.\n\n<br>\n\n",
        "briefDescription": "The scheme aims to provide innovative, effective and integrated training opportunities for work force who need new skills to enjoy the dignity that comes with employment, independence and self-reliance.",
        "detailedDescription": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The scheme \"Advanced Vocational Training Scheme (AVTS)\" has been launched by the Directorate General of Training (DGT), Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship, Government of India. It aims to upgrade and update the skills of the industrial workforce through short-term modular training. Through this scheme, short-term training courses of 1 to 6 weeks are provided to industrial workers, technicians, supervisors, engineers, instructors, and technical students for skill upgradation. The scheme is implemented by National Skill Training Institutes (NSTIs) under the Directorate General of Training (DGT), including NSTIs at Mumbai, Kanpur, Howrah, Hyderabad (Vidyanagar), Chennai, Hyderabad (Ramanthapur), Ludhiana, Dehradun, Calicut, Bangalore, Jamshedpur, and other centres. The training is offered in selected skill areas through regular and tailor-made courses designed as per the requirements of industries and establishments. The institute is equipped with workshops, laboratories, hostel facilities, and other infrastructure to support training. The scheme was launched in collaboration with UNDP/ILO and is delivered through modular courses to meet the training demands of industries and institutions."
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "bold": true,
                "text": "Mission:",
                "underline": true
              }
            ],
            "type": "block_quote"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "To continuously upgrade the skills of the industrial workforce for higher productivity"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "list_item"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Bridging the gap between academics and industries for suitable placement for the young generation in technical fields"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "list_item"
              }
            ],
            "type": "ul_list"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "bold": true,
                "text": "Objective:",
