              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "Step 1: "
                },
                {
                  "text": "The applicant should approach a Member Lending Institution (MLI) for obtaining financial assistance under the scheme. The MLI shall identify and provide financial assistance/loans to suitable and eligible Scheduled Caste entrepreneurs/beneficiaries."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "Step 2: "
                },
                {
                  "text": "The applicant should submit the loan application and required documents to the MLI for appraisal and due diligence. The MLI shall evaluate the credit application using prudent banking judgment and select commercially viable proposals."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "Step 3: "
                },
                {
                  "text": "After approval of the loan, the MLI shall issue a valid Sanction Letter/Letter of Intent (LoI) to the Scheduled Caste beneficiary, enterprise, company, firm, society, sole proprietorship firm, or individual."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "Step 4: "
                },
                {
                  "text": "The MLI shall register the loan application with IFCI Limited after agreeing in principle to extend the loan to the Scheduled Caste beneficiary. The MLI may submit the application through the CEGSSC web portal, after which an acknowledgement/token number will be generated."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "Step 5: "
                },
                {
                  "text": "The MLI shall submit the required details to IFCI, including the valid sanction letter/Letter of Intent issued to the beneficiary/enterprise/company/firm/society/sole proprietorship firm/individual."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "Step 6: "
                },
                {
                  "text": "The MLI shall disburse the sanctioned loan amount to the eligible applicant. Within 30 days of the first disbursement, the MLI shall submit the sanction letter, proof of disbursement, guarantee fee, and compliance certificate to IFCI."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
