          "process_md": "> **Registration Guidelines for farmers:**\n\n\n\n   1. Users can register by Clicking [**here**](http://enam.gov.in/NAMV2/home/other_register.html).   1. Select \u201cRegistration Type\u201d as \u201cFarmer\u201d and select the desired \u201cAPMC\u201d.\n   1. Provide a valid email ID, as you will receive your Login ID and Password on it.\n   1. Once successfully registered, you will receive a login ID and a temporary password at the given email.\n   1. Log in to the dashboard by clicking the icon on [**www.enam.gov.in/web**](https://www.enam.gov.in/web/).    1. You will see a flashing message on the dashboard: \u201cClick here to register with APMC.\u201d\n   1. Click on the flashing link, which will redirect you to the registration page for filling or updating details.\n   1. Your application will be sent for approval to your selected APMC after KYC is completed.\n   1. After successfully logging in to your dashboard, you will be able to see all APMC address details.\n   1. After successful submission, the user will receive an email confirming that the application has been submitted to the concerned APMC, with the status shown as Submitted, In Progress, Approved, or Rejected.\n   1. Once approved by the APMC, you will receive your eNAM Farmer Permanent Login ID (e.g., HR866F00001) and password for complete access to the e-NAM platform at your registered email address.\n   1. Alternatively, you can contact your respective Mandi/APMC for the same.\n\n\n> **Registration Guidelines for Trades:**\n\n\n\n   1. Users will have to register by visiting [**http://enam.gov.in/NAMV2/home/other_register.html**](http://enam.gov.in/NAMV2/home/other_register.html)**.**   1. Select \u201cRegistration Type\u201d as \u201cTrader\u201d and choose the appropriate \u201cAPMC\u201d or State Level option. \n   1. Provide your passport-size photograph and correct email ID to receive your login ID and password at the same address.\n   1. After successful registration, you will receive your login ID and a temporary password at your provided email ID.\n   1. Log in to the dashboard by clicking the icon on [**www.enam.gov.in**](https://www.enam.gov.in/web/).   1. Then you will see a flashing message on the dashboard: \u201cClick here to register with APMC.\u201d\n   1. Click on the flashing link, which will redirect you to the registration page for filling or updating details.\n   1. Your application will be submitted for approval to your selected APMC or SAMB (in case of a Unified License).\n   1. After successfully logging in to your dashboard, you will be able to see the arrivals and trade activities happening in the APMC for notified commodities in eNAM.\n   1. You will see a flashing message on the dashboard: \u201cClick on the link.\u201d\n   1.  It will redirect you to the registration page to submit your license and KYC details as a trader.\n   1. Your details will be submitted for approval by your selected APMC.\n   1. Once successfully submitted, you will receive an email confirming the status of the application as Submitted, In Progress, Approved, or Rejected.\n   1. Its status can be viewed by logging in to the dashboard, as explained earlier.\n   1. For a permanent login ID (e.g., HR866T00001) and password, visit your respective Mandi/APMC and verify your license number.\n   1. After successful approval by the APMC, eNAM Trader/CA IDs and passwords will be sent to the provided email address.\n   1. Trader/CA users can participate in online trade using the provided login ID and password.\n\n\n<br>\n\n> **For FPOs/FPCs:** FPOs/FPCs can register on e-NAM Portal via the website ([**www.enam.gov.in**](https://www.enam.gov.in/web/)) or mobile app or provide following details at the nearest e-NAM mandi:\n\n\n\n   1. Name of your FPOs/FPCs.\n   1. Name, address, email ID, and contact number of the authorized person (MD/CEO/Manager).\n   1. Bank account details (Name of bank, branch, account number, IFSC code).\n\n\n<br>\n\n> **For Mandi Board:** States (State Agricultural Marketing Boards) interested in integrating their mandis with NAM are required to carry out the following reforms in their APMC Act:\n\n\n\n   1. Provide for a single (unified) trading license valid across the state.\n   1. Implement a single-point levy of market fees across the state.\n   1. Include provisions for e-auction/e-trading as modes of price discovery.\n\n\n<br>\n\n",
          "url": ""
        }
