        "detailedDescription_md": "The &quot;e-National Agriculture Market (e-NAM)&quot; is a pan-India electronic trading platform launched on 14th April 2016 to integrate APMC mandis across the country under the \u201cOne Nation One Market\u201d initiative. Implemented by the Small Farmers Agribusiness Consortium (SFAC) under the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers\u2019 Welfare, the platform provides online trading facilities for agricultural commodities. It offers services such as commodity arrival information, quality assaying, e-bidding, and direct e-payment to farmers through a single-window system. The scheme aims to improve transparency, efficiency, and better price discovery in agricultural marketing. In Jammu &amp; Kashmir, 11 mandis have been integrated with the e-NAM platform since May 2020.\n<br>\n\n",
