        "benefits_md": "> **Honorarium:**\n\n\n- Honorarium of \u20b950,000/- per month is provided to the Emeritus Professor.\n\n> **Contingency Grant:**\n\n\n- A non-lapsable contingency grant of \u20b91,00,000/- per annum is provided.\n- The grant may be used for secretarial assistance, stationery, postage, consumables, books, journals, and travel related to the approved assignment.\n- The grant may also be used for attending one scientific meeting or conference within India per year.\n- Economy-class airfare, admissible daily allowance, and road mileage are allowed from the contingency grant.\n- No separate Travel Allowance (TA) or Daily Allowance (DA) is provided.\n- The grant is released based on requisition and actual utilization of the previous year&#39;s grant.\n- Books and journals purchased from the grant become the property of the concerned university or college.\n- The contingency grant may be enhanced with the concurrence of the Financial Adviser (Department of Agricultural Research and Education), depending on the assignment.\n\n> **Academic and Institutional Support:**\n\n\n  - The Emeritus Professor is entitled to medical and other facilities available to university faculty members.\n  - The Emeritus Professor remains attached to an Agricultural University, ICAR Deemed University, or another eligible institution that provides the required facilities.\n\n> **Research and Professional Engagement**\n\n\n- The Emeritus Professor is provided an opportunity to continue approved academic, research, and professional activities in agriculture and allied sciences.\n\n<br>\n\n",
        "briefDescription": "The ICAR floated the Scheme of Emeritus Professor in order to provide an opportunity to the superannuated teachers/ Scientists of universities, colleges and institutions under ICAR-AU System. \n",
        "detailedDescription": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "align": "justify",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The \"ICAR Emeritus Professor Scheme\" is implemented by the Indian Council of Agricultural Research (ICAR), Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare, to utilise the expertise and services of outstanding superannuated teachers and scientists from the National Agricultural Research and Education System (NARES). The scheme provides an opportunity to retired professionals to undertake teaching, training, student research guidance, and other academic activities in agricultural universities and institutions. It supports the development of instructional materials, textbooks, and e-learning resources for use in national agricultural education programmes and distance education. The scheme aims to address shortages in faculty positions, strengthen agricultural education, and leverage the experience of retired experts in addressing nationally important academic and policy issues. It also encourages retired teachers and scientists to contribute to higher agricultural education, particularly in economically and ecologically underprivileged regions."
