                        }
                      ],
                      "link": "https://web.umang.gov.in/web_new/home",
                      "type": "link"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " "
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "The citizen can login using mobile number and OTP."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Once logged In, citizen can search for NSAP."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Click on \u201cApply Online\u201d"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Fill the basic details, choose the mode of payment of pension, upload photo and click on \u201cSubmit\u201d."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                }
              ],
              "type": "ul_list"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "process_md": "\n- One can download UMANG App or visit website [https://web.umang.gov.in/web_new/home](https://web.umang.gov.in/web_new/home) - The citizen can login using mobile number and OTP.\n- Once logged In, citizen can search for NSAP.\n- Click on \u201cApply Online\u201d\n- Fill the basic details, choose the mode of payment of pension, upload photo and click on \u201cSubmit\u201d.\n\n<br>\n\n",
          "url": "https://web.umang.gov.in/web_new/home "
        },
        {
          "mode": "Offline",
          "process": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Individuals can submit completely filled applications to the Gram Panchayat / Block Office in the rural area and the Municipality / Municipal Council in the urban area, as per eligibility."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "A Verification Officer or Verification Team under an authorized officer verifies the applications with reference to facts related to eligibility"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "The Verification Officer make the necessary recommendation for sanction or rejection with reasons."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "The list of applicants with the recommendations of the Verifying Authority is discussed in the Gram Sabha in rural areas or Ward Sabha / Area Sabha as designated by the State Government in urban areas and thereafter in the Gram Panchayats and Municipalities."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "If the time limits are not adhered to by Gram Sabha / Ward Sabhas, Gram Panchayats / Municipalities the Verification Officer directly submits his recommendations to the Sanctioning Authority under intimation to the Gram Panchayat / Municipality."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "After receipt of applications which are verified and recommended by the Gram Sabha / Ward Committee / Area Sabha, the Sanctioning Authority convey approval to the applicant in the form of a Sanction Order with a copy to Gram Panchayat / Municipality concerned."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "The Sanctioning Authority issues Sanction Order under his seal"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Every beneficiary who has been sanctioned pension under schemes of NSAP are issued a Pension Passbook. The Passbook contain details of the Sanction Order, particulars of the pensioner and disbursement details"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "The list of beneficiaries to whom sanctions are issued is displayed at the Gram Panchayat / Ward / Municipal Office and updated every three months. "
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "The Pension amount is directly paid to the beneficiaries through the Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) process to their post office or bank account."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "list_item"
                }
              ],
              "type": "ul_list"
            }
          ],
          "process_md": "\n- Individuals can submit completely filled applications to the Gram Panchayat / Block Office in the rural area and the Municipality / Municipal Council in the urban area, as per eligibility.\n- A Verification Officer or Verification Team under an authorized officer verifies the applications with reference to facts related to eligibility\n- The Verification Officer make the necessary recommendation for sanction or rejection with reasons.\n- The list of applicants with the recommendations of the Verifying Authority is discussed in the Gram Sabha in rural areas or Ward Sabha / Area Sabha as designated by the State Government in urban areas and thereafter in the Gram Panchayats and Municipalities.\n- If the time limits are not adhered to by Gram Sabha / Ward Sabhas, Gram Panchayats / Municipalities the Verification Officer directly submits his recommendations to the Sanctioning Authority under intimation to the Gram Panchayat / Municipality.\n- After receipt of applications which are verified and recommended by the Gram Sabha / Ward Committee / Area Sabha, the Sanctioning Authority convey approval to the applicant in the form of a Sanction Order with a copy to Gram Panchayat / Municipality concerned.\n- The Sanctioning Authority issues Sanction Order under his seal\n- Every beneficiary who has been sanctioned pension under schemes of NSAP are issued a Pension Passbook. The Passbook contain details of the Sanction Order, particulars of the pensioner and disbursement details\n- The list of beneficiaries to whom sanctions are issued is displayed at the Gram Panchayat / Ward / Municipal Office and updated every three months. \n- The Pension amount is directly paid to the beneficiaries through the Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) process to their post office or bank account.\n\n",
