          "process_md": "**Step 1: Apply for Entrance Examination**\n\n1. Candidates seeking admission to the M.V.Sc. programme must apply for the All India Competitive Examination conducted by the Indian Council of Agricultural Research, New Delhi.\n1. Candidates applying for the Ph.D. programme must submit an application form through the Indian Veterinary Research Institute website after the admission advertisement is released.\n1. Applicants must carefully select the subject for the entrance examination and submit the application before the prescribed last date.\n\n**Step 2: Appear in the Entrance Examination**\n\n1. Eligible candidates must appear in the competitive written entrance examination conducted on an All India basis.\n1. The examination consists of multiple-choice questions and is conducted in English only.\n1. Ph.D. entrance examinations are conducted at various IVRI campuses and regional stations, including Bareilly, Bangalore, Bhopal, Kolkata, and Palampur.\n\n**Step 3: Merit List, Counseling, and Admission**\n\n1. Admission is granted on the basis of marks obtained in the entrance examination and fulfillment of minimum qualifying marks.\n1. For the M.V.Sc. programme, final selection and counseling are conducted by ICAR based on merit.\n1. For the Ph.D. programme, the merit list is prepared according to written examination marks, followed by tie-breaking based on MVSc marks, BVSc marks, and age.\n1. Selected candidates are admitted to the programme and become eligible for the IVRI Scholarship.\n\n<br>\n\n",
