        "eligibilityDescription_md": "**IVRI Institute Scholarship for M.V.Sc. and Ph.D.**\n\n- The applicant must be admitted to the M.V.Sc. or Ph.D. programme through a competitive entrance examination conducted by the Indian Veterinary Research Institute.\n- Candidates must maintain a minimum CGPA of 7.00 out of 10.00 at the end of each semester to continue receiving the scholarship.\n\n**For Master\u2019s (M.V.Sc.) Programme**\n\n- The applicant must possess a Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Veterinary Science in the relevant discipline as specified by the Veterinary Council of India.\n- Candidates must have secured at least 60% aggregate marks or equivalent CGPA.\n- A minimum of 55% marks is required for SC/ST and sponsored candidates.\n\n**For Doctoral (Ph.D.) Programme**\n\n- The applicant must possess an M.V.Sc. degree in the relevant discipline from a recognized university in India.\n- General/OBC candidates must have a minimum CGPA of:\n\n6.50 out of 10.00 scale, or\n3.25 out of 5.00 scale, or\n2.60 out of 4.00 scale.\n\n- SC/ST/Physically Challenged/Sponsored candidates must have a minimum CGPA of:\n\n5.50 out of 10.00 scale, or\n2.75 out of 5.00 scale, or\n2.20 out of 4.00 scale.\n\n- Where only marks are awarded, General/OBC candidates must have at least 60% marks, while SC/ST/Physically Challenged/Sponsored candidates must have at least 50% marks.\n\n**Age Limit**\n\n- The minimum age for Ph.D. candidates is 23 years as on 1st August of the academic session.\n- There is no upper age limit.\n\n<br>\n\n"
