    "en": {
      "applicationProcess": [
        {
          "mode": "Offline",
          "process": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "Step 1: "
                },
                {
                  "text": "The application for registration may be given on plain paper to the local Gram Panchayat. An individual may appear personally before the Panchayat Secretary or Gram Rozgar Sahayak and make an oral request for registration, in which case the particulars required will be noted by the Gram Rojgar Sahayak or the Panchayat Secretary. "
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Application for registration should contain names of those adult members of the household who are willing to do unskilled manual work. Particulars such as age, sex, SC/ST status, Rashtriya Swastha Bima Yojana (RSBY) number, Aadhar number, Below Poverty Line (BPL) status and bank/post office account number (if s/he has opened one) must be provided in the application."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "Step 2:"
                },
                {
                  "text": " The Gram Panchayat (GP) will verify the following details:"
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Whether the household is really an entity as stated in the application."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Whether the applicant household are local residents in the Gram Panchayat concerned."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Whether applicants are adult members of the household."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "The process of verification shall be completed as early as possible, and in any case not later than a fortnight after the receipt of the application in the Gram Panchayat."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "Step 3:"
                },
                {
                  "text": " All particulars of a household found to be eligible after verification, will be entered in the MIS (NREGASoft) by the Panchayat Secretary or the Gram Rojgar Sahayak (GRS) or a person duly authorized by the State Government."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "Step 4:"
                },
                {
                  "text": " If a household is found to be eligible for registration, the GP will, within a fortnight of the application, issue a JC to the household. JC should be handed over to one of the members of the applicant household in the presence of a few other residents of the GP. The format of the Job Card is provided in the Annexure-5 of the scheme guidelines."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "The detailed format for application for registration is provided in Annexure-3 of the scheme guidelines."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "* Registrations shall be opened throughout the year at the Gram Panchayat (GP) office."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "* Application for registration must be made on behalf of the household by any adult member."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "process_md": "**Step 1:** The application for registration may be given on plain paper to the local Gram Panchayat. An individual may appear personally before the Panchayat Secretary or Gram Rozgar Sahayak and make an oral request for registration, in which case the particulars required will be noted by the Gram Rojgar Sahayak or the Panchayat Secretary. \nApplication for registration should contain names of those adult members of the household who are willing to do unskilled manual work. Particulars such as age, sex, SC/ST status, Rashtriya Swastha Bima Yojana (RSBY) number, Aadhar number, Below Poverty Line (BPL) status and bank/post office account number (if s/he has opened one) must be provided in the application.\n**Step 2:** The Gram Panchayat (GP) will verify the following details:\nWhether the household is really an entity as stated in the application.\nWhether the applicant household are local residents in the Gram Panchayat concerned.\nWhether applicants are adult members of the household.\nThe process of verification shall be completed as early as possible, and in any case not later than a fortnight after the receipt of the application in the Gram Panchayat.\n**Step 3:** All particulars of a household found to be eligible after verification, will be entered in the MIS (NREGASoft) by the Panchayat Secretary or the Gram Rojgar Sahayak (GRS) or a person duly authorized by the State Government.\n**Step 4:** If a household is found to be eligible for registration, the GP will, within a fortnight of the application, issue a JC to the household. JC should be handed over to one of the members of the applicant household in the presence of a few other residents of the GP. The format of the Job Card is provided in the Annexure-5 of the scheme guidelines.\n**The detailed format for application for registration is provided in Annexure-3 of the scheme guidelines.**\n*** Registrations shall be opened throughout the year at the Gram Panchayat (GP) office.**\n*** Application for registration must be made on behalf of the household by any adult member.**\n",
          "url": ""
        },
        {
          "mode": "Online - via CSC",
          "process": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Individuals should also be given the option to make registration to apply for registration at other touch points such as Community Service Centre (CSC). The CSC operator will fill in the details in the application form and forward the filled application form to the concerned GP for necessary action. State Government will issue necessary enabling orders in this regard."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "* Registrations shall be opened throughout the year at the Gram Panchayat (GP) office."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "bold": true,
                  "text": "* Application for registration must be made on behalf of the household by any adult member."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "process_md": "Individuals should also be given the option to make registration to apply for registration at other touch points such as Community Service Centre (CSC). The CSC operator will fill in the details in the application form and forward the filled application form to the concerned GP for necessary action. State Government will issue necessary enabling orders in this regard.\n*** Registrations shall be opened throughout the year at the Gram Panchayat (GP) office.**\n*** Application for registration must be made on behalf of the household by any adult member.**\n",
