          ],
          "answer_md": "The assistance will be provided to such surviving member of the household of the deceased poor , who after local inquiry, is found to be the head of the household.\n",
          "question": "How will it be decided which member of the family should be provided the amount of assistance be provided?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Under this scheme, a household will receive a one-time assistance of \u20b9 20000."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "Under this scheme, a household will receive a one-time assistance of [?] 20000.\n",
          "question": "What is the maximum amount of financial assistance that a household can receive through NFBS?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Yes, Your mother will be considered as the Primary Breadwinner. Irrespective of the gender, the Primary Breadwinner is the family member whose income constitutes a major share of the family\u2019s total earnings."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "Yes, Your mother will be considered as the Primary Breadwinner. Irrespective of the gender, the Primary Breadwinner is the family member whose income constitutes a major share of the family's total earnings.\n",
          "question": "My mother passed away this month. She and my father were both earning members of the family. However, my mother earned more than my father. Will she be considered as the Primary Breadwinner of the family? "
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "No, the term \u201chousehold\u2019 in this case strictly includes spouse, minor children, unmarried daughters and dependent parents."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "No, the term \"household' in this case strictly includes spouse, minor children, unmarried daughters and dependent parents.\n",
          "question": "Will my uncles & aunts and their children will also be considered as part of the household?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "The duly filled and signed form (along with the copies of the required documents) need to be submitted to either the District Social Welfare Officer (DSWO) or Tehsil Social Welfare Officer (TSWO)."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "The duly filled and signed form (along with the copies of the required documents) need to be submitted to either the District Social Welfare Officer (DSWO) or Tehsil Social Welfare Officer (TSWO).\n",
          "question": "I have duly filled and signed the application form for NFBS. I have also attached the necessary documents and passport sized photograph. Where/Whom am I supposed to submit the form?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Yes, for the applicant who is unable to sign the form, there is the option for providing the thumb impression."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "Yes, for the applicant who is unable to sign the form, there is the option for providing the thumb impression.\n",
          "question": "After my father passed away, my mother became the main breadwinner of the family. She is eligible to apply for NFBS but she is illiterate and cannot sign. Does the form has the option of thumb impression instead of signature?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "The details reg. the Family ID and Member ID can be found in your BPL Card."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
