        "detailedDescription_md": "The scheme &quot;National Pension Scheme For Traders And Self-Employed Persons&quot; was launched by the Ministry of Labour and Employment, Government of India. The scheme aims to provide old age protection and social security to small-scale traders, retailers, and self-employed individuals. The scheme provides a voluntary and contributory pension under which the beneficiary receives a minimum assured monthly pension of \u20b93,000/- after attaining the age of sixty years, along with matching contributions from the Government of India. The applicant must make monthly contributions ranging between \u20b955/- and \u20b9200/- per month till they attain the age of 60 years.\n<br>\n\n",
