        "benefits_md": "\n- \u20b9200 per month for beneficiaries aged 60\u201379 years.\n- \u20b9500 per month for beneficiaries aged 80 years and above.\n\n> **Note:** At present old age beneficiaries are getting anywhere between \u20b9200/- to \u20b91000/- depending on the State Contribution.\n\n<br>\n\n",
        "briefDescription": "\"Indira Gandhi National Old Age Pension Scheme\" is one of the five sub-schemes of the National Social Assistance Programme. Under IGNOAPS, citizens living Below Poverty Line and 60 years or above in age are eligible to apply. A monthly pension of \u20b9 200 up to 79 years and \u20b9 500 thereafter.",
        "detailedDescription": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The \"Indira Gandhi National Old Age Pension Scheme (IGNOAPS)\" is one of the five sub-schemes of the National Social Assistance Programme, Ministry of Rural Development. Under this scheme, persons belonging to BPL households and 60 years or above in age are eligible to apply. This program is being implemented in rural areas as well as urban areas. "
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The Government of India, on 15th August 1995, introduced the National Social Assistance Programme (NSAP) as a fully funded Centrally Sponsored Scheme targeting the destitute, defined as any person who has little or no regular means of subsistence from his/her own source of income or through financial support from family members or other sources. "
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "bold": true,
                "text": "The NSAP at present includes five sub-schemes as its components- "
