      "schemeDefinitions": [
        {
          "definition": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "A beneficiary family will comprise husband, wife and unmarried [sons and/ or unmarried daughters.]"
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "The beneficiary family should not own a pucca house (an all weather dwelling unit) either in his/her name or in the name of any member of his/her family in any part of India."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "[An adult earning member (irrespective of marital status) can be treated as a separate household;"
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Provided that he /she does not own a pucca house (an all weather dwelling unit) in his /her name in any part of India."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Provided also that in the case of a married couple, either of the spouses or both together in joint ownership will be eligible for a single house, subject to income eligibility of the household under the Scheme.]1"
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "[Further, such person with pucca house having built-up area less than 21 sq.m may be included for enhancement of existing dwelling units upto 30 sq.m. However, if enhancement is not possible on account of lack of availability of land/ space or any other reason, she/ he may get a house under PMAY(U) elsewhere.]"
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "definitions_md": "A beneficiary family will comprise husband, wife and unmarried [sons and/ or unmarried daughters.]\nThe beneficiary family should not own a pucca house (an all weather dwelling unit) either in his/her name or in the name of any member of his/her family in any part of India.\n<br>\n\n[An adult earning member (irrespective of marital status) can be treated as a separate household;\nProvided that he /she does not own a pucca house (an all weather dwelling unit) in his /her name in any part of India.\nProvided also that in the case of a married couple, either of the spouses or both together in joint ownership will be eligible for a single house, subject to income eligibility of the household under the Scheme.]1\n<br>\n\n[Further, such person with pucca house having built-up area less than 21 sq.m may be included for enhancement of existing dwelling units upto 30 sq.m. However, if enhancement is not possible on account of lack of availability of land/ space or any other reason, she/ he may get a house under PMAY(U) elsewhere.]\n",
