        "benefits_md": "&lt;br&gt;\n\n**States/UTs****BLC &amp;amp;amp;amp; AHP****ARH****ISS**Assam, Arunachal Pradesh, Meghalaya, Manipur, Mizoram, Nagaland, Tripura, Sikkim, Himachal Pradesh, Uttarakhand, UTs of Jammu and Kashmir, Puducherry, and DelhiCentral Govt. - \u20b92.25 lakh/Unit;   State Govt. - Min. \u20b90.25 lakh/UnitTechnology Innovation Grant Central Govt. - \u20b93,000/sqm per unit State Govt.- \u20b92,000/sqm per unit Home Loan Subsidy \u2013 up to \u20b91.80 lakh (Actual Release) per unit by the Government of India as a Central Sector SchemeAll other UTsCentral Govt. - \u20b92.50 lakh/UnitDoDoAll other StatesCentral Govt. - \u20b91.5 lakh/Unit;    State Govt. - Min. \u20b91.00 lakh/UnitDoDo<br>\n\n<br>\n\n",
        "briefDescription": "Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana - Urban (PMAY-U) Scheme was launched on 25th June 2015 by the Hon\u2019ble Prime Minister to provide all-weather pucca houses to all eligible urban households across the nation with the vision of \u2018Housing for All\u2019. ",
        "detailedDescription": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The \u201cPradhan Mantri Awas Yojana \u2013 Urban (PMAY-U)\u201d was launched on 25th June 2015 by the Ministry of Housing & Urban Affairs, Government of India with the vision of \u201cHousing for All\u201d to provide pucca houses to eligible urban households. Implemented by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs, the scheme addresses urban housing shortages, especially for EWS, LIG, and MIG categories, including slum dwellers. It promotes affordable and sustainable housing through components like the Credit Linked Subsidy Scheme (CLSS), offering interest subsidies on housing loans. The mission covers all statutory towns and notified urban areas as per Census 2011. Aadhaar is mandatory for all eligible beneficiaries under the scheme."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "align_justify"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          }
        ],
        "detailedDescription_md": "The \u201cPradhan Mantri Awas Yojana \u2013 Urban (PMAY-U)\u201d was launched on 25th June 2015 by the Ministry of Housing &amp;amp; Urban Affairs, Government of India with the vision of \u201cHousing for All\u201d to provide pucca houses to eligible urban households. Implemented by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs, the scheme addresses urban housing shortages, especially for EWS, LIG, and MIG categories, including slum dwellers. It promotes affordable and sustainable housing through components like the Credit Linked Subsidy Scheme (CLSS), offering interest subsidies on housing loans. The mission covers all statutory towns and notified urban areas as per Census 2011. Aadhaar is mandatory for all eligible beneficiaries under the scheme.\n<br>\n\n",
