          "process_md": "##### ***Registration Process For Establishments***\n**Step 1:** The employer must access the official portal of the Employees&#39; Provident Fund Organisation to initiate the deemed registration process for their existing or newly covered establishment. The establishment must ensure its standard records are fully compliant with current statutory mandates. \n**Step 2:** The employer must update and accurately provide their unique Permanent Account Number, Goods and Services Tax Network details, and a Permanent Account Number linked Bank Account Number within the portal to facilitate direct benefit transfers.\n<br>\n\n##### ***Registration Process For Employees*** \n**Step 1:** The employee must download and access the official UMANG Mobile Application on their smartphone to begin the registration process and securely generate a Universal Account Number for the scheme. \n**Step 2:** The employee must utilize the Facial Authentication Technology facility provided within the UMANG Application to authenticate their identity and successfully link their Aadhaar to the new Universal Account Number.\n<br>\n\n##### ***Application Process For Benefits Disbursement***\n**Step 1:** The establishment must accurately file the monthly Electronic Challan-cum-Return along with the prescribed amount of provident fund contributions for all eligible newly joined employees and re-joinees through the designated online return portal. \n**Step 2:** The establishment must ensure the continuous filing of the Electronic Challan-cum-Return for six completed wage months to successfully trigger the automated six-monthly lump sum benefit calculation and subsequent disbursement process.\n<br>\n\n##### ***Post-Application Processes*** \n**Step 1:** The first-time employee must log in to the Employees&#39; Provident Fund Organisation employee portal and successfully complete the mandatory online Financial Literacy Course to become fully eligible for the second installment of their designated incentive.\n**Step 2:** The applicant can track their application and file any grievances related to eligibility or non-receipt of incentives using the online grievance redressal facility and escalation matrix provided by the Employees&#39; Provident Fund Organisation, ensuring resolution within fifteen days.\n<br>\n\n##### ***Grievance Redressal / Help &amp; Support***\nThe Employees&#39; Provident Fund Organisation provides an online facility and a dedicated call center for the Pradhan Mantri Viksit Bharat Rozgar Yojana to assist stakeholders and resolve grievances within fifteen days.\n(Note: A specific internet &quot;SOURCES&quot; table was omitted as all information was exclusively derived from the provided document guidelines.)\n<br>\n\n"
