          ],
          "answer_md": "Establishments with pending inquiries under Sections 7A, 7B, or 7C of the Employees&#39; Provident Funds and Miscellaneous Provisions Act, 1952, will not be provided with any employer incentives until cleared.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "What happens if my business is currently facing pending legal inquiries regarding compliance issues related to provident fund regulations?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "To qualify as a first-time employee, you must not have been a contributing member of the Employees' Provident Fund Organisation or an Exempted Trust prior to the commencement of this initiative."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "To qualify as a first-time employee, you must not have been a contributing member of the Employees&#39; Provident Fund Organisation or an Exempted Trust prior to the commencement of this initiative.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "Suppose I have previously made contributions to a provident fund through a past employer before joining this new job. Will I still qualify for the direct financial assistance given to fresh entrants in the workforce?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Re-joining workers must ensure their Universal Account Number is securely Aadhaar Authenticated by utilizing either biometric scanning or facial authentication technology to be eligible."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "Re-joining workers must ensure their Universal Account Number is securely Aadhaar Authenticated by utilizing either biometric scanning or facial authentication technology to be eligible.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "As an individual who already has a previous contributory membership and is now re-joining the workforce, what specific verification steps do I need to take regarding my personal account number?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Small businesses with a baseline of fewer than 50 employees must create a minimum of 2 sustained additional employments over their established baseline to qualify for the employer support benefits."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "Small businesses with a baseline of fewer than 50 employees must create a minimum of 2 sustained additional employments over their established baseline to qualify for the employer support benefits.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "For a smaller enterprise that currently has an average historical workforce of fewer than fifty workers, what is the exact minimum number of new hires required to start receiving the wage support benefits?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Fresh entrants must have a gross wage of up to \u20b91,00,000/- per month at the time of joining the registered establishment to remain eligible for the financial assistance."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "Fresh entrants must have a gross wage of up to \u20b91,00,000/- per month at the time of joining the registered establishment to remain eligible for the financial assistance.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "Is there any specific maximum threshold regarding the starting monthly salary that a fresh graduate joining their first official employment should be aware of to ensure they remain eligible for the support?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Businesses against which a First Information Report has been filed by the Employees' Provident Fund Organisation for fraudulent practices are strictly excluded from receiving any incentives."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "Businesses against which a First Information Report has been filed by the Employees&#39; Provident Fund Organisation for fraudulent practices are strictly excluded from receiving any incentives.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "If our company was previously flagged for certain irregularities and currently has an active police complaint filed by the provident fund authorities regarding past fraudulent activities, can we still apply for the employer support?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "You must authenticate your Universal Account Number utilizing the Facial Authentication Technology available on the UMANG mobile application to be eligible for the first-timer incentives."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "You must authenticate your Universal Account Number utilizing the Facial Authentication Technology available on the UMANG mobile application to be eligible for the first-timer incentives.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "When creating my new unique account number to start receiving my initial employment benefits, what specific technology must be used on the official mobile application to properly verify my identity?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Employers must consistently file the monthly Electronic Challan-cum-Return along with the prescribed amount of provident fund contributions for their employees on a regular basis."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "Employers must consistently file the monthly Electronic Challan-cum-Return along with the prescribed amount of provident fund contributions for their employees on a regular basis.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "In order to maintain active eligibility and continue receiving the promised financial incentives for generating new jobs, what specific monthly compliance action must the employer ensure is completed without fail?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "The payment of incentives will immediately cease in the event that a newly hired beneficiary leaves their employment either voluntarily or under other circumstances."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "The payment of incentives will immediately cease in the event that a newly hired beneficiary leaves their employment either voluntarily or under other circumstances.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "What exactly occurs to the financial support being provided to a new worker if they decide to resign from their current position at the company before the full benefit period is completed?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Establishments with a baseline of 50 or more employees are required to generate at least 5 additional employments over and above their baseline to trigger the employer incentives."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "Establishments with a baseline of 50 or more employees are required to generate at least 5 additional employments over and above their baseline to trigger the employer incentives.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "If our manufacturing firm already employs over sixty individuals on average, how many extra sustained positions must we successfully generate above our usual staffing levels to participate in the employment creation initiative?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Workers in seasonal industries must continue with the exact same establishment for the entire continuous period of 6 months to fulfill the eligibility criteria for the initial payment."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "Workers in seasonal industries must continue with the exact same establishment for the entire continuous period of 6 months to fulfill the eligibility criteria for the initial payment.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "For those of us who are taking up initial employment in a sector that only operates during certain seasons of the year, what are the specific criteria regarding continuous work to qualify for the first installment?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Yes, any enterprise that has pending or decided inquiries relating to irregularities under the Atmanirbhar Bharat Rojgar Yojana, or any other government scheme, is explicitly excluded from receiving benefits."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "Yes, any enterprise that has pending or decided inquiries relating to irregularities under the Atmanirbhar Bharat Rojgar Yojana, or any other government scheme, is explicitly excluded from receiving benefits.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "We previously participated in the Atmanirbhar Bharat Rojgar Yojana and currently have an unresolved inquiry regarding our compliance with that specific program. Will this affect our current eligibility as an employer?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "First-time employees are required to successfully complete the mandatory online Financial Literacy Course made available through the Employees' Provident Fund Organisation portal to become eligible for the second installment."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "First-time employees are required to successfully complete the mandatory online Financial Literacy Course made available through the Employees&#39; Provident Fund Organisation portal to become eligible for the second installment.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "Besides completing the mandatory twelve months of continuous service with my company, what specific educational requirement must I finish on the official online portal to unlock the second portion of my incentive payment?"
        },
        {
          "answer": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Individuals who joined their respective establishments prior to 01.08.2025 are classified as old employees, and employers will not receive any financial benefits for retaining them."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "answer_md": "Individuals who joined their respective establishments prior to 01.08.2025 are classified as old employees, and employers will not receive any financial benefits for retaining them.\n<br>\n\n",
          "question": "If a worker was already officially hired by the company and on the payroll sometime in June 2025, can the employer still claim the monthly additionality benefits for continuing to employ this specific person?"
        }
      ]
    },
