        "detailedDescription_md": "The National Savings (Monthly Income Account) Scheme, 2019, popularly known as the Post Office Monthly Income Scheme (POMIS), is a government-backed small savings scheme administered by the Ministry of Finance. The scheme provides a fixed monthly income to investors through periodic interest payments on a one-time deposit made at the time of account opening. The scheme is designed for individuals seeking a secure investment option with regular monthly returns. Accounts can be opened individually, jointly by up to three adults, or on behalf of eligible minors.\n> **Key Features**\n\n\n- Government-backed savings scheme with assured returns.\n- Single deposit account with no recurring contributions.\n- Monthly interest payout to the account holder.\n- Account tenure of 5 years.\n- Joint accounts permitted with up to three adults.\n- Nomination facility available as per applicable rules.\n- Transfer of an account from one post office to another is permitted.\n- Multiple accounts may be opened subject to the prescribed deposit limits.\n\n<br>\n\n",
