        "benefits_md": "***Financial Assistance Rates***\n\n- Class I to IV (for the purchase of dress/books, etc.): \u20b91,000/- per annum.\n- Class V to VIII: \u20b91,500/- per annum.\n- Class IX: \u20b92,000/- per annum.\n- Class X: \u20b92,000/- per annum.\n- Class XI to XII: \u20b93,000/- per annum.\n- ITI: \u20b96,000/- per annum.\n- Polytechnic: \u20b96,000/- per annum.\n- Degree Courses (including B.Sc. Agriculture): \u20b96,000/- per annum.\n- Professional Courses: \u20b925,000/- per annum.\n\n***Mode of Disbursement:*** The benefits under the scheme are transferred through the Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) system.\n<br>\n\n",
        "briefDescription": "The scheme aims to fund the pre-matric and post-matric education of wards belonging to specific mine, beedi, and cine workers. It provides annual scholarships between \u20b91,000/- and \u20b925,000/- based on the student's academic level and course type.",
        "detailedDescription": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The scheme \"Financial Assistance for Education to the Wards of Beedi/Cine/IOMC/LSDM Workers \u2013 Pre & Post-Matric\" was launched by the Ministry of Labour & Employment, Government of India. The scheme aims to provide educational scholarships to the children of Beedi, Iron Ore, Manganese & Chrome Ore, Limestone, Dolomite, Mica, and Cine workers. The scheme provides annual financial assistance ranging from \u20b91,000/- to \u20b925,000/- directly to the beneficiaries via Direct Benefit Transfer. The applicant must be studying in a recognized institution and meet the stipulated parental occupation and income thresholds. The applications for this scheme are accepted online through the National Scholarship Portal."
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          }
        ],
        "detailedDescription_md": "The scheme &quot;Financial Assistance for Education to the Wards of Beedi/Cine/IOMC/LSDM Workers \u2013 Pre &amp; Post-Matric&quot; was launched by the Ministry of Labour &amp; Employment, Government of India. The scheme aims to provide educational scholarships to the children of Beedi, Iron Ore, Manganese &amp; Chrome Ore, Limestone, Dolomite, Mica, and Cine workers. The scheme provides annual financial assistance ranging from \u20b91,000/- to \u20b925,000/- directly to the beneficiaries via Direct Benefit Transfer. The applicant must be studying in a recognized institution and meet the stipulated parental occupation and income thresholds. The applications for this scheme are accepted online through the National Scholarship Portal.\n<br>\n\n",
        "exclusions": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "bold": true,
                "text": "The scholarship sanctioned is liable to be canceled on the following occasions - ",
                "underline": true
              }
            ],
            "type": "block_quote"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "If the scholar is found to have obtained a scholarship by false statements."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "list_item"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "If the scholarship discontinues his/her studies, the scholarship shall be stopped from the date of such discontinuance."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "list_item"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "If the scholar changes the subject of the course of study for which the scholarship was originally awarded or changes the Institution of Study without the prior approval of the Welfare Commissioner."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "list_item"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "If the scholar fails to make satisfactory progress in the studies or is irregular in attendance or is guilty of misconduct during the academic year for which the scholarship has been granted."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "list_item"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "If the parent(s) of the scholar ceases to be a Beedi/Mine/Cine worker."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "list_item"
              }
            ],
            "type": "ol_list"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "bold": true,
                "text": "The following category of students is not eligible for the award of scholarships under the scheme - ",
                "underline": true
              }
            ],
            "type": "block_quote"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Students who, after passing one stage of education, are studying in the same stage of education in a different subject. e.g. B.Sc. after B.Com. or B.Com. after B.A. or M.A. in one subject after M.A. in another subject."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "list_item"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Students who after having completed their educational career in one professional line, continue education in a different professional line, e.g. L.L.B. after B.T. or B.Ed."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "list_item"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The Scholars pursuing studies through Correspondence are not eligible."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "list_item"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Students who receive scholarships or stipends from any other source will not be granted under this Scheme. "
