        "detailedDescription_md": "The scheme &amp;quot;ICMR-Junior Research Fellowship&amp;quot; by the Department of Health Research (DHR), Ministry Of Health &amp;amp; Family Welfare, Government of India, aims to enhance the availability of trained health research personnel through providing short-term training fellowships and financial assistance to medical faculty and researchers. It supports training in both Indian and foreign institutions for a duration of 1-3 months. The scheme focuses on priority areas such as clinical trials, genomics, toxicology, and biotechnology. It encourages multidisciplinary collaboration and the development of research projects addressing national and local health challenges. The fellowship also aims to build a skilled workforce in advanced medical and health research domains.\n<br>\n\n",
